6 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205035 #edb/ref 1061 476517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205035 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1b8a4ffe-a6bc-5748-9925-775d621ef0ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205035 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186205174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205036 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205036 #edb/ref 1061 476518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205036 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2a517a1e-2402-5834-92c6-d387d20f3740" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205036 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205037 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205037 #edb/ref 1061 476521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205037 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a4d784bb-4dc8-51b7-9c57-1caf81eeaf95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205037 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186205208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205038 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205038 #edb/ref 1061 476522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205038 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "15db0382-7d51-5840-b3da-75384a89354d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205038 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186205207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205039 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205039 #edb/ref 1061 476523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205039 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8211e280-4fa1-564c-9189-09c44ee53dde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205039 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205040 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205040 #edb/ref 1061 476526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205040 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "16595ce8-f055-561b-9a7f-397923fee1b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205040 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205041 #edb/ref 1061 476529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205041 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eddfa8ae-b5d6-5ef0-ba45-f6c57207ae16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205041 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205174 #edb/ref 1064 "Some linear equations can have **no solutions.** This means there is no value of $x$ that can be substituted into the equation to give a true statement.\n\nFor example, let's consider the following equation:\n\n$$\nx+1 = x\n$$\n\nLet's attempt to solve this equation. We start by subtracting $x$ from both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =x \\\\ x+1\\,-\\,x & =x\\,-\\,x \\\\ (x-x)+1 & =(x-x) \\\\ 0+1 & =0 \\\\ 1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the final equation, $1=0,$ is always **false**. In other words, there is no value of $x$ that we can substitute to make the equation true. \n\nTherefore, our equation has no solutions." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205174 #edb/ref 1065 11390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205174 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ae552721-c050-5d83-9cfc-347accbc894b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205174 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205207 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n7qx = -5,\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solutions, what is the value of $q?$\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax = b{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{7q}_{\\large a} \\ x = \\underbrace{-5}_{\\large b}\n$$\n\nIn this case,\n\n$$\na = 7q, \\qquad b = -5.\n$$\n\nWe know that an equation of the form $ax=b$ with $b \\neq 0$ has no solutions when $a = 0.$\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n7q = 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7q & =0 \\\\ \\frac{7q}{7} & =\\frac{0}{7} \\\\ q & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the equation $7qx = -5$ has no solutions if $q = 0.$\n\n**Note:** The constant $q$ in this problem is sometimes called a **parameter.**" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205207 #edb/ref 1065 13402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205207 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d31382b3-ae61-5a9e-a3bf-53f71f939a5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205207 #edb/ref 1067 "Problems Involving Unknown Parameters" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205208 #edb/ref 1064 "In general, suppose we have an equation in the variable $x$ of the form \n\n$$\nax = b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $a$ and $b$ are constants, and\n\n- $b$ is *not* equal to zero, which we write as $b \\neq 0.$\n\nThen, if $a = 0,$ the equation has **no solutions.**\n\nIndeed, by substituting $a = 0$ into $ax=b,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ax & =b \\\\ (0)x & =b \\\\ 0 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a *contradiction* (i.e., a statement that's always false) because we were told that $b \\neq 0.$ Therefore, the equation has no solution." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205208 #edb/ref 1065 13428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205208 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8a5cc3be-1b56-5e46-8944-f75697b65b59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205208 #edb/ref 1067 "Conditions for an Equation To Have No Solutions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234237 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186570579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234237 #edb/ref 1069 "q-67439" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234237 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234237 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $-\\frac{2}{x+3}=\\frac{8}{x-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234237 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aa75fc9d-104d-5e12-b331-4d8ff3973336" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234237 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we note that\n\n- $x=-3$ cannot be a solution since this would make the denominator on the left-hand side zero\n\n- $x=1$ cannot be a solution since this would make the denominator on the right-hand side zero\n\nWe can flip an equation involving two fractions as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{c}{d}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{d}{c}\n$$\n\nThe above technique works whenever $a$ and $c$ are both different from zero.\n\nTherefore, we can flip the given equation as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{x+3}{2}=\\frac{x-1}{8}\n$$\n\nNext, we write both fractions using the least common denominator, $8.$ The equation becomes\n\n$$\n-\\frac{4x+12}{8}=\\frac{x-1}{8}.\n$$\n\nWe can now solve this equation with the addition and the multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)\\cdot \\frac{4x+12}{-8} & =(-8)\\cdot \\frac{x-1}{8} \\\\ 4x+12 & =-x+1 \\\\ 4x+x & =1-12 \\\\ 5x & =-11 \\\\ (\\frac{1}{5})\\cdot (5x) & =(\\frac{1}{5})\\cdot (-11) \\\\ (\\cancel{\\frac{1}{5}})\\cdot (\\cancel{5}x) & =(\\frac{1}{5})\\cdot (-11) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{11}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250824 #edb/ref 1080 "images/11/1115307cc21acb99416f137a4e79ef0f2e93ca284db1006d968fed3afebc803c.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250824 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250824 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1ffa339d-52f0-58f8-a4c8-c7ef06bd326f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251377 #edb/ref 1080 "images/3c/3c73d16ae2282e64f22ab933eb20e877fcfdbc8c4e9412d79d54c2ab0f7bf6d9.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251377 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251377 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "64bb6df6-798f-5abb-8b24-d116b26ad066" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251624 #edb/ref 1080 "images/6e/6e87bcbdd832273540492f632614159f67012eefdbc391649f06ce4ef9138421.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251624 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251624 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7f667702-f9d0-511e-8700-d4c8b184082b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251956 #edb/ref 1080 "images/dc/dcc13cd2dd9978670a522d994a00521e44fe57ca1a26250f14093caa460aa26b.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251956 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251956 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a2dea51b-15d5-5fe8-8958-491e3d895dfd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252760 #edb/ref 1080 "images/73/737e030ba35f922fc67ed421bec7c072e5d2b6b2d1fda11d2f081453b541d4a8.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252760 #ed