ab9-bb4fe4e92884" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477030 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $az=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(p+2)z-8 & =-3 \\\\ (p+2)z-8+8 & =-3+8 \\\\ {{(p+2)}_{⏟}}_{a}z & ={{5}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\np+2=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p+2 & =0 \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477031 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186477029 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477031 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477031 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $w,$ given by\n\n$$\n5(r-5)w-6=4\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477031 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "353a2e9f-97dd-52cc-88ff-dcca6d9658cb" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477031 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $aw=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(r-5)w-6 & =4 \\\\ 5(r-5)w-6+6 & =4+6 \\\\ {{5(r-5)}_{⏟}}_{a}w & ={{10}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n5(r-5)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(r-5) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{5(r-5)}{5} & =\\frac{0}{5} \\\\ r-5 & =0 \\\\ r & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477034 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186477038 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477034 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477034 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $v,$ given by\n\n$$\n2(q+5)v+6=-4\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$\n\n$q=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477034 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "498d8977-f2e3-576d-98c6-e159e4faf155" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477034 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $av=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(q+5)v+6 & =-4 \\\\ 2(q+5)v+6-6 & =-4-6 \\\\ {{2(q+5)}_{⏟}}_{a}v & ={{-10}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2(q+5)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(q+5) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(q+5)}{2} & =\\frac{0}{2} \\\\ q+5 & =0 \\\\ q & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477035 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186477037 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477035 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477035 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n7(p-3)z-8=2\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477035 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4a5d0c30-0fb9-5290-b84c-1e98357759f7" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477035 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $az=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(p-3)z-8 & =2 \\\\ 7(p-3)z-8+8 & =2+8 \\\\ {{7(p-3)}_{⏟}}_{a}z & ={{10}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n7(p-3)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(p-3) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{7(p-3)}{7} & =\\frac{0}{7} \\\\ p-3 & =0 \\\\ p & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477039 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186477041 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477039 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477039 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $w,$ given by\n\n$$\n(r-3)w-6=-5\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477039 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a5dfc3bd-e99d-5c7f-b114-d44a00e9f10d" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477039 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $aw=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-3)w-6 & =-5 \\\\ (r-3)w-6+6 & =-5+6 \\\\ {{(r-3)}_{⏟}}_{a}w & ={{1}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nr-3=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r-3 & =0 \\\\ r & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477042 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186204091.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477042 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "e10796af-bb63-5d21-97c0-87246139b4f3" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477046 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186477071 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477046 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477046 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $v,$ given by\n\n$$\n3nv=6v+6\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $n?$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477046 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1eca6787-bc49-5086-8428-52d3acf41f5a" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477046 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $av=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $6v$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3nv & =6v+6 \\\\ 3nv-6v & =6v+6-6v \\\\ 3nv-6v & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $v$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(3n-6)v=6.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $av=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(3n-6)}_{⏟}}_{a}v={{6}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n3n-6=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $n,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n-6 & =0 \\\\ 3n-6+6 & =0+6 \\\\ 3n & =6 \\\\ \\frac{3n}{3} & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\ n & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443]}
